<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Years of Lead (Italy)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1969–<a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Anni di piombo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/years-of-lead-morocco">Years of Lead</a> (anni di piombo) were a period of political violence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from the late 1960s to the 1980s. Far-left groups such as the Red <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigade">Brigades</a> and neo-fascist groups carried out bombings, shootings and kidnappings, including the Piazza Fontana bombing of 1969, the kidnapping and murder of the former prime minister Aldo Moro in 1978 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> station bombing of 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/years-of-lead-italy.jpg" alt="Years of Lead (Italy)" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Bramfab at Italian Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anni_di_piombo2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
